  "258": {
    "inputs": {
      "value": "subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is the overall visual style established by <Picture 1>, a hand-drawn 1980s Shanghai Animation Film Studio cel style with simple clean ink linework, flat minimal color fills, and a plain hand-painted texture.\n\nsummary:\n[reference generation] The target video is an eight-second extreme wide shot panning across a snow-covered Chinese New Year lantern festival in an ancient Gusu city at night. The whole video follows the minimalist 1980s Shanghai Animation Film Studio look defined by <Subject 1>, which is referenced from <Picture 1>.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1> (appears in [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - the target video consistently carries the simple clean linework, flat minimal coloring, and hand-painted texture of <Subject 1> throughout the entire shot.\n\ndetailed_description:\nThe target video is a 2D-animated piece in the 1980s Shanghai Animation Film Studio style defined by <Subject 1>, with simple clean ink outlines, flat understated color fills, and a plain painted texture.\n[Shot 1] An extreme wide shot frames an ancient Gusu city under nightfall, its full length of streets decorated with rows of red paper lanterns hanging from snow-covered eaves. The snow-dusted bluestone street catches a faint silvery glow from the lantern light. The camera pans right with large amplitude at slow speed, sweeping steadily from the left edge to the right edge of the festival in the simple 2D visual language of <Subject 1>. Simplified pedestrians wrapped in winter coats cross the foreground in opposite directions, their smooth hand-drawn outlines staying flat and economical; farther back, small silhouettes drift among the lanterns. In the distance the lantern chain stretches away like a glowing red river. Distant voices, drumbeats, and children's laughter mingle softly, and a barely distinct vendor's call hawking candied sugar-hawn skewers rises somewhere in the distance before fading as the camera continues moving.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nA warm holiday crowd murmurs and laughs beneath distant gongs and drums, with children shouting playfully. Light footsteps scuff across the snowy stone, and a faraway vendor's hawking call for candied sugar-hawn skewers rises briefly and fades as the camera pans right.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nA light bamboo-flute melody at a moderate tempo with gentle ornamentation, subtly cheerful and buoyant, playing steadily underneath the entire scene without growing in volume."
    },
